cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ABI: Provenance-Preserving Capability Acquisition and Segregation"
message: "If you use ABI or build on these results, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yoder
    given-names: Sam
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yoder23/abi"
license: "Apache-2.0"
version: "0.3.0-alpha.1"
date-released: "2026-08-24"
abstract: >
  ABI is a research compiler for acquiring measured capabilities from frozen
  open-weight language models, segregating linguistic form from specialist
  knowledge, accounting for imported information, and producing immutable
  acquisition artifacts for external execution hosts.
keywords:
  - large-language-models
  - knowledge-transfer
  - capability-segregation
  - provenance
  - pytorch
  - transformers
